    "markdown": "---\npagetitle: \"Cross Validation\"\neditor: source\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    html-math-method: mathjax\n    chalkboard: true\n    incremental: true\n    theme: [default, custom.scss]\n    height: 900\n    width: 1600\n    slide-number: c\n    auto-stretch: false\n    callout-appearance: simple\n    pdf-max-pages-per-slide: 2\n    menu:\n      side: right\n      numbers: true\nexecute:\n  echo: true\n  warning: false\n  message: false\n---\n\n\n\n::::: columns\n::: {.column .center width=\"55%\"}\n![](img/tidymodels.png){width=\"90%\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.column .center width=\"45%\"}\n<br>\n\n[Cross Validation]{.custom-title}\n\n<br> <br> <br> <br> <br> \n\n[Grayson White]{.custom-subtitle}\n\n[Stat 243 <br> Week 4 \\| Fall 2026]{.custom-subtitle}\n:::\n:::::\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n## Goals for today (and next time)\n\n:::: {.columns}\n\n::: {.column width='50%'}\n\n::: {.nonincremental .fragment}\n\n**Today:**\n\n-   Wrap up linear regression\n-   Start cross validation\n\n:::\n\n:::\n\n::: {.column width='50%'}\n\n::: {.nonincremental .fragment}\n\n**Wednesday:**\n\n-   Bootstrapping\n\n\n:::\n\n:::\n\n::::\n\n\n\n# Linear Regression Wrap-Up\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n### Linear Regression\n\nModel Form:\n\n$$ \n\\begin{align}\ny &= \\beta_o + \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2 + \\cdots + \\beta_p x_p + \\epsilon\n\\end{align}\n$$\n\nLinear regression is a flexible class of models that allow for:\n\n::: nonincremental\n-   Both quantitative and categorical **explanatory** variables.\n\n-   **Multiple** explanatory variables.\n\n-   **Curved** relationships between the response variable and the explanatory variable.\n\n-   BUT the **response variable is quantitative**.\n:::\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### More time with the `palmerpenguins`!\n\n![](img/penguins.png){fig-align=\"center\"}\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Recap: Regression with the penguins so far\n\n**One Quantitative Variable**\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(palmerpenguins)\nlibrary(moderndive)\nmod <- lm(bill_length_mm ~ bill_depth_mm, data = penguins)\n\nget_regression_table(mod)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 2 × 7\n  term          estimate std_error statistic p_value lower_ci upper_ci\n  <chr>            <dbl>     <dbl>     <dbl>   <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>\n1 intercept        55.1      2.52      21.9        0   50.1     60.0  \n2 bill_depth_mm    -0.65     0.146     -4.46       0   -0.936   -0.363\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Recap: Regression with the penguins so far\n\n**One Categorical Variable**\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(palmerpenguins)\nlibrary(moderndive)\nmod <- lm(bill_length_mm ~ species, data = penguins)\n\nget_regression_table(mod)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 3 × 7\n  term               estimate std_error statistic p_value lower_ci upper_ci\n  <chr>                 <dbl>     <dbl>     <dbl>   <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>\n1 intercept             38.8      0.241     161.        0    38.3     39.3 \n2 species: Chinstrap    10.0      0.432      23.2       0     9.19    10.9 \n3 species: Gentoo        8.71     0.36       24.2       0     8.01     9.42\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: nonincremental\n-   Estimated regression line for $x_2 = 1$:\n\n<br>\n\n-   Estimated regression line for $x_2 = 0$:\n:::\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Recap: Regression with the penguins so far\n\n**Equal Slopes Model**\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(palmerpenguins)\nlibrary(moderndive)\nmod <- lm(bill_length_mm ~ species + bill_depth_mm, data = penguins)\n\nget_regression_table(mod)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 4 × 7\n  term               estimate std_error statistic p_value lower_ci upper_ci\n  <chr>                 <dbl>     <dbl>     <dbl>   <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>\n1 intercept             13.2      2.25       5.88       0     8.80    17.6 \n2 species: Chinstrap     9.94     0.368     27.0        0     9.22    10.7 \n3 species: Gentoo       13.4      0.512     26.2        0    12.4     14.4 \n4 bill_depth_mm          1.39     0.122     11.4        0     1.15     1.63\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: nonincremental\n-   Estimated regression line for $x_2 = 1$:\n\n<br>\n\n-   Estimated regression line for $x_2 = 0$:\n:::\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### Recap: Regression with the penguins so far\n\n\n**Different Slopes Model**\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nlibrary(palmerpenguins)\nlibrary(moderndive)\nmod <- lm(bill_length_mm ~ species*bill_depth_mm, data = penguins)\n\nget_regression_table(mod)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 6 × 7\n  term                    estimate std_error statistic p_value lower_ci upper_ci\n  <chr>                      <dbl>     <dbl>     <dbl>   <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>\n1 intercept                 23.1       3.02       7.65   0       17.1      29.0 \n2 species: Chinstrap        -9.64      5.72      -1.69   0.093  -20.9       1.60\n3 species: Gentoo           -5.84      4.54      -1.29   0.199  -14.8       3.08\n4 bill_depth_mm              0.857     0.164      5.22   0        0.534     1.18\n5 species: Chinstrap:bil…    1.06      0.31       3.44   0.001    0.455     1.68\n6 species: Gentoo:bill_d…    1.16      0.279      4.17   0        0.615     1.71\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: nonincremental\n-   Estimated regression line for $x_2 = 1$:\n\n<br>\n\n-   Estimated regression line for $x_2 = 0$:\n:::\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### This time: Regression with multiple quantitative predictors\n\n\n:::: {.columns}\n\n::: {.column width=50%}\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nggplot(penguins, aes(x = body_mass_g, y = bill_length_mm)) +\n  geom_point()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](stat243_wk04mon_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){fig-align='center' width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n::: {.column width=50%}\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nggplot(penguins, aes(x = bill_depth_mm, y = bill_length_mm)) +\n  geom_point()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](stat243_wk04mon_files/figure-revealjs/unnamed-chunk-7-1.png){fig-align='center' width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n:::\n\n::::\n\n\n::: {.fragment}\n\n$$\ny = \\beta_o + \\beta_1x_{\\textrm{Bill Depth}} + \\beta_2 x_{\\textrm{Body Mass}} + \\epsilon\n$$\n\n:::\n\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n### This time: Regression with multiple quantitative predictors\n\nIn R:\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmod <- lm(bill_length_mm ~ bill_depth_mm + body_mass_g, penguins)\nget_regression_table(mod)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 3 × 7\n  term          estimate std_error statistic p_value lower_ci upper_ci\n  <chr>            <dbl>     <dbl>     <dbl>   <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>\n1 intercept       23.3       3.27       7.14   0       16.9     29.7  \n2 bill_depth_mm    0.163     0.137      1.19   0.234   -0.106    0.432\n3 body_mass_g      0.004     0         12.6    0        0.004    0.005\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Visualizing the best fit plane\n\n\n::: {.cell layout-align=\"center\"}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\noptions(rgl.useNULL = TRUE)\noptions(rgl.printRglwidget = TRUE)\nlibrary(rgl)\nplot3d(x = penguins$bill_depth_mm, y = penguins$body_mass_g, \n       z = penguins$bill_length_mm, type = \"s\", col = \"goldenrod\", size = 1)\nplanes3d(a = coef(mod)[2], b = coef(mod)[3], c=-1, d = coef(mod)[1], alpha = .5)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<style>#rgl28859 {margin:auto;}</style>\n<div id=\"rgl28859\" style=\"width:960px;height:480px;\" class=\"rglWebGL html-widget\" role=\"img\" aria-labelledby=\"rgl28859-aria\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"rgl28859\">{\"x\":{\"material\":{\"color\":\"#000000\",\"alpha\":1,\"lit\":true,\"ambient\":\"#000000\",\"specular\":\"#FFFFFF\",\"emission\":\"#000000\",\"shininess\":50,\"smooth\":true,\"front\":\"filled\",\"back\":\"filled\",\"size\":3,\"lwd\":1,\"fog\":true,\"point_antialias\":false,\"line_antialias\":false,\"texture\":null,\"textype\":\"rgb\",\"texmode\":\"modulate\",\"texmipmap\":false,\"texminfilter\":\"linear\",\"texmagfilter\":\"linear\",\"texenvmap\":false,\"depth_mask\":true,\"depth_test\":\"less\",\"isTransparent\":false,\"polygon_offset\":[0,0],\"margin\":\"\",\"floating\":false,\"tag\":\"\",\"blend\":[\"src_alpha\",\"one_minus_src_alpha\"]},\"rootSubscene\":1,\"objects\":{\"8\":{\"id\":8,\"type\":\"spheres\",\"material\":{},\"vertices\":\"0\",\"colors\":\"1\",\"radii\":[[34.64212036132812]],\"centers\":\"2\",\"ignoreExtent\":false,\"fastTransparency\":true,\"flags\":32771},\"10\":{\"id\":10,\"type\":\"text\",\"material\":{\"lit\":false,\"margin\":0,\"floating\":true,\"edge\":[0,1,1]},\"vertices\":\"3\",\"colors\":\"4\",\"texts\":[[\"penguins$bill_depth_mm\"]],\"cex\":[[1]],\"adj\":[[0.5,0.5,0.5]],\"centers\":\"5\",\"family\":[[\"sans\"]],\"font\":[[1]],\"ignoreExtent\":true,\"flags\":33808},\"11\":{\"id\":11,\"type\":\"text\",\"material\":{\"lit\":false,\"margin\":1,\"floating\":true,\"edge\":[1,1,1]},\"vertices\":\"6\",\"colors\":\"7\",\"texts\":[[\"penguins$body_mass_g\"]],\"cex\":[[1]],\"adj\":[[0.5,0.5,0.5]],\"centers\":\"8\",\"family\":[[\"sans\"]],\"font\":[[1]],\"ignoreExtent\":true,\"flags\":33808},\"12\":{\"id\":12,\"type\":\"text\",\"material\":{\"lit\":false,\"margin\":2,\